<title>USA: Champion Enterprises Inc Q1 full results.</title>
<headline>Champion Enterprises Inc Q1 full results.</headline>
<dateline>AUBURN HILLS, Mich. 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollars in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>						   Q1 Ended  Q1 Ended</p>
<p>						    Mar 29,  Mar 30,    %</p>
<p>						    1997     1996  Change</p>
<p>Net sales:</p>
<p> Housing					 $362,957 $328,624  10%</p>
<p> Commercial vehicles			   15,903   14,141  12%</p>
<p> Total net sales				378,860  342,765  11%</p>
<p> Cost of sales				  323,087  290,794  11%</p>
<p> Selling, general and admin. expenses    32,836   29,257  12%</p>
<p> Operating income (2)			  22,937   22,714   1%</p>
<p> Interest income, net				 2	216</p>
<p> Income before income taxes		  22,939   22,930</p>
<p> Income taxes (3)				 9,100    9,188 (1%)</p>
<p> Net income					13,839   13,742   1%</p>
<p> Net income per share (4)			0.28     0.28</p>
<p>Weighted average shares outstanding (in 000's) (4)</p>
<p>						     49,673   49,242</p>
<p>NOTE: (1) On October 24, 1996 Redman Industries Inc merged with Champion. Merger accounted for as pooling of interests; accordingly, 1996 restated information includes Redman. (2) Commercial vehicles had operating income of $353,000 and $732,000 in quarters ended March 29, 1997 and March 30, 1996, respectively. Decrease in income is attributed to lower profits associated with municipal orders. (3) Income tax provisions have been calculated using annual effective rate method. Difference between taxes at 35 percent federal statutory rate and taxes provided for the periods presented is due to state and foreign tax charges. (4) Prior year amounts have been restated for the effect of the two-for-one stock split on May 31, 1996.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
